From: =?UTF-8?q?Martin=20=C5=A0trobl?= <recordyletsplays@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:03:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rfs: Fix the size of an NV item read response

ipc_rfs_nv_data_item_size_setup() returned the size of the response
header alone, so ipc_rfs_nv_read_item_setup() allocated a buffer without
room for the item and then copied the item behind it.
---
 samsung-ipc/rfs.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/samsung-ipc/rfs.c b/samsung-ipc/rfs.c
index c9cee1b..1616f89 100644
--- a/samsung-ipc/rfs.c
+++ b/samsung-ipc/rfs.c
@@ -713,7 +713,7 @@ size_t ipc_rfs_nv_data_item_size_setup(
 	if (header == NULL || nv_data == NULL || nv_size == 0)
 		return 0;
 
-	size = sizeof(struct ipc_rfs_nv_read_item_response_header) + size;
+	size = sizeof(struct ipc_rfs_nv_read_item_response_header) + nv_size;
 
 	return size;
 }
